# Template for the Pad .env — DO NOT put real values in this file.
#
# deploy.sh renders the real .env (mode 600, never committed) from
# ../../secrets/pm-stack.sops.yaml. This template exists so the shape
# of the configuration is reviewable in git. Key names match the SOPS
# file; deploy.sh performs the mapping noted beside each entry.

# The API authenticates with user-scoped `pad_` tokens minted in
# the instance (`pad token create`, secret shown once) — there is no
# server-env API key on this version. The automation token for this
# stack is SOPS: pad_api_token, also filed in Bitwarden +
# 1Password as `pad.api-token` (see ../README.md). Nothing to
# render here today; deploy.sh still renders an (empty-by-design)
# .env so the compose env_file contract stays uniform across the
# stack.
